 ### [Adaptive Octree Marching Tetrahedra](3897-adaptive-octree-marching-tetrahedra.md)
-Adaptive Octree Marching Tetrahedra uses an adaptive octree to subdivide a 3D volume only where the scalar field contains the target isovalue. At leaf nodes (1x1x1 cubes), the volume is decomposed into tetrahedra, and the Marching Tetrahedra algorithm is applied to generate the mesh. It solves the problem of inefficient uniform-grid processing by reducing memory usage and computational cost for sparse or complex datasets. Unlike Naive Isosurface Extraction which processes every voxel, this method explicitly constructs an octree data structure to manage resolution adaptivity before decomposing leaf nodes into tetrahedra for precise surface intersection.
